w7-robot-clearance.solution:
### 1. Represent the robot as link segments

FK must give the position of **all joints**, not just the end effector. Two consecutive joints $p_i,p_{i+1}$ form one segment. Compute the point-to-segment distance to each segment and take the minimum:

$$d_{\min}=\min_i d(O,[p_i,p_{i+1}]).$$

This works because the closest point on the chain lies on at least one of the segments. Distance only to the joint points could miss a collision in the middle of a link.

### 2. Implement projection, clamping and minimum

~~~python
import numpy as np

def point_segment_distance(point, start, end):
    point, start, end = [np.asarray(p, dtype=float) for p in (point, start, end)]
    segment = end - start
    length_sq = segment @ segment
    if length_sq == 0.0:
        return np.linalg.norm(point - start)
    t = ((point - start) @ segment) / length_sq
    t = np.clip(t, 0.0, 1.0)
    closest = start + t * segment
    return np.linalg.norm(point - closest)

def robot_clearance(joint_positions, obstacle):
    if len(joint_positions) < 2:
        raise ValueError("Minst to leddposisjoner er nødvendig")
    return min(
        point_segment_distance(obstacle, a, b)
        for a, b in zip(joint_positions[:-1], joint_positions[1:])
    )
~~~

### 3. Hand-computed check

Take an arm with joints $(0,0)$, $(2,0)$ and $(2,2)$, and obstacle $O=(1,1)$. On the first link $t=2/4=0.5$, closest point $(1,0)$ and distance 1. On the second link also $t=0.5$, closest point $(2,1)$ and distance 1. Thus the minimum distance is 1, not $\sqrt2$ as the distance to the nearest joint point would give.

If a link has zero length, it reduces to a point. The code handles this without division by zero. All points must be expressed in the same frame and length unit.

### Limitation: geometry is not a full collision guarantee

For a capsule model with link radius $r_i$ and a circular obstacle with radius $r_O$ the clearance is $\min_i(d_i-r_i-r_O)$. A negative value means overlap. With radius 0.1 for both link and obstacle the example gives clearance $1-0.1-0.1=0.8$. Also check between waypoints: collision-free endpoints do not guarantee a collision-free motion.
